Historical 2019 build notes
==========================

See README.md for the Python 3 port and tested CUDA 13 nested-loop path.
The requirements below describe the original full runtime distribution.

Pre-requisites
--------------

Python 2.7
CUDA 10 (8 or 9 may work)
Kepler or newer NVIDIA graphics card


Software pre-requisites
-----------------------

* CUB (v1.8)

https://github.com/NVlabs/cub

(Older versions *might* work, but have not been tested. Minimum version is CUB 1.3.1)

* ModernGPU (v1.1)

https://github.com/NVlabs/moderngpu/releases


Create symlinks to the above in rt/include directory.

  $ ln -s path-to-cub-x.y/cub
  $ ln -s path-to-mgpu-x.y/ mgpu


* Python requirements

The requirements below can be installed using `pip` as:

    pip install --system -r requirements.txt
    
Note the use of the `--system` flag -- this is very important if you
are on a shared home directory with multiple host architectures since
pip doesn't seem to handle multiarch very well.

If you do *not* use such configurations (shared home directory, multiple
host architectures), then you can use the `--user` flag if you don't
have root access.

    pip install --user -r requirements.txt

[NOTE TO LOCAL USERS: In particular, these packages are already
available on the pyx subnet and should *not* be reinstalled.]

** Manual installation

If you prefer to manually install code, use the instructions below.

*** cgen

Pick revision 697deaca4ff6c4cd2789b07c5096b5fc2ea6c581 or later (2015.1.1+).

https://github.com/inducer/cgen.git

Or 

  pip install cgen

Or if you don't have root privileges
  
  pip install cgen --user

*** pycparser (2.09.1 or later)

https://github.com/eliben/pycparser/releases

Or
	
  pip install pycparser

*** toposort (1.0 or later)

https://pypi.python.org/pypi/toposort


Make
----

$ cd $GGC
$ make

This should make the runtime as well compile the sample programs in bmks.


Inputs
------

$ cd $GGC
$ ln -s /path/to/inputs inputs

Within ISS, /path/to/inputs is /net/ohm/export/cdgc/inputs

Within PYX, /path/to/inputs is /nfs/hen2-10/shared/sree/inputs

Running
-------

Change to the gensrc/$bmk directory, and run 

$ make
$ ./test /path/to/graph/file

Example:

$ cd $GGC/gensrc/bfs-topo
$ ./test /path/to/NY.gr -o output-NY

For an automated system that can run, verify and gather performance
data for each benchmark, see README.bmk2.
